// Phase 71 Plan 02 Task 1 (EVAL-01-a; CONTEXT D-04): the run condition is a
// new dimension of the seeded ABBA schedule.
//
// - buildSchedule without conditions is byte-identical to the Phase 66
//   function: it deep-equals the committed V1 schedule fixture, generated by
//   the unedited code, and no entry carries a `condition` key.
// - With conditions, slots are (arm, condition) pairs in ABBA order and the
//   run id ends in -<arm>-<condition>.
// - The task permutation depends only on mulberry32(seed + round), so seed 66
//   with conditions ['off'] reproduces V1's task order round by round.
// - condition_not_applied is a pausing infra code; jev_measurement_missing is
//   a run flag.
//
// Phase 71 Plan 03 Task 1 (EVAL-01-a; CONTEXT D-04, D-11; RESEARCH Pattern 2,
// Pitfalls 7-10): the runner applies the condition and proves it.
// - --conditions and --gate are validated with every other option; the dry
//   run lists the conditions only when they are given.
// - Before each run and outside the timed window, the switch is written
//   through the MCP settings tool and read back over CDP, with the capture
//   arm; a mismatch or an unverifiable read is condition_not_applied, the
//   arm never runs and the campaign pauses.
// - The preflight refuses --conditions on a build without the settings key,
//   with an armed capture, or when CDP cannot verify anything.
// - Raw records are schema 2 (condition, jevMeasurement, endReason, safety,
//   evidence.dropped), and an 'on' run waits for jevMeasurement only when its
//   run_task fast_mode summary reports Jev attempts.
// - The gate's sha256 and the conditions join the identity a resume must keep.
//
// Phase 71 Plan 05 Task 2 (EVAL-02; CONTEXT D-11 and its 2026-10-16
// amendment): --gate loads the file through the gate's exact-key validator
// (gate_invalid lists only error codes), the dry run prints gateSha256, and
// the "gate campaign preflight" refuses gate_campaign_mismatch in --campaign
// mode, fresh or resumed, before any client opens.
//
// Fakes only: no MCP server, no browser, no host CLI, no socket. The 71-03
// tests write only under os.tmpdir().
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
